Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	## Safety / regression evidence
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- **Contracts and risk:** High-risk ownership/concurrency change affecting `durable-ack`, `recovery-generation`, `reader-snapshot`, `historical-input` and `query-meaning`. Preserve admission, formats, isolation and configured durability; intentionally add explicit handle outcomes and documented disposal/error contracts. [API and migration guide](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/blob/19065cc1e/docs/transaction-handles.md).
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- **Prior states and interactions:** Direct/Shared; ordinary, legacy and handle calls; concurrent handles and live cursors; pooled hosts; maintenance/close; encrypted/historical files; external writers; abandoned sessions; reused wrappers with fresh cores. Inherited recovery, compatibility and fuzz coverage remains required.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- **Failure outcomes:** Acknowledged commits survive the stated fault models; rolled-back writes stay absent; uncertain commits remain indeterminate. Close cancels blocked admission before draining work, and maintenance permits existing dependencies to finish. Cleanup preserves its own errors without repeating a peer's fatal error. External writes become visible after reacquisition and cold reopen. Shared parent final checkpointing remains explicitly best-effort; pin/child errors propagate after cleanup.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- **Evidence:** Sixteen registered comparisons: eight against actual `560529066`, three against actual `eb01f346e`, three against actual `e821ae747`, and two against published packages. Permanent guards, registered fault hooks, coverage dispositions and runtime/platform checks accompany them. The final production tree passes **658 relevant tests on each net8/net10**, zero failures/skips; the final allocation harness passes **13 cases on each runtime**. Independent combined late-reader/facade review passes **58 cases per runtime**. Counts overlap. All production library targets build; net462/net481 tests compile. All **96 CI-policy tests** pass. Current runs: [CI and Safety evidence](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/actions/runs/36710337230), [16 regression proofs](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/actions/runs/36710336868), [Fuzz](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/actions/runs/36710336954), [index compatibility](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/actions/runs/36710336973), [Shared production comparisons](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/actions/runs/36710336824). These must finish on this exact head, including actual CLR 4 and native platforms. [Finite gate and detailed dispositions](https://github.com/JKamsker/LiteDB/blob/19065cc1e/docs/transaction-handles-safety-review.md); the immutable archive will be linked after hosted validation completes.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	- **Coverage delta and residual concerns:** Replacements and CI/harness changes are recorded in the ledger; no new quarantine. Native partitions preserve the exact selection and reject missing/duplicate/empty results; discovery now matches VSTest case sensitivity. The pin-progress test deliberately replaces a combined startup/throughput budget with bounded startup and completed-write progress, a 60-second overall cap, held-pin negative controls and exact cold-state assertions. Its original Windows timeout remains **unknown in origin**, with no retrospective deadlock or runner-slowdown claim. The strongest counterexample is close/maintenance preventing a continuation it needs; forced interleavings, genuine-error controls and before/after proofs address it. Existing quarantines remain gaps. Evidence covers exceptions, process death and modeled persistence faults, not physical power removal. This is the affected PR's finite #3034 gate, not completion of the whole roadmap or repository protection/merge-queue configuration; post-merge validation is configured, not claimed executed.
