Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	Four fresh processes per strategy/caller count, three seconds warmup and five seconds measurement; every ID, payload, indexed result and unrelated sentinel is checked on two cold reopens. Single-caller Direct measured 187.0 writes/s; the zero-linger queue 186.7, the 1ms batching queue 154.6 and IPC batching 150.4. **Linger costs roughly 18–20% at low load.** Sampled peak WAL at sixteen callers is ~13.4 MiB Direct, ~13.1 MiB existing coordinator, ~8 MiB queued/IPC and <0.5 MiB Shared; checkpoint/close schedules and in-flight transactions differ. Full ranges, client/server CPU, allocation and drain measurements are in the report. IPC client allocation excludes the server.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	**Semantics and limits:** this prototype coalesces immutable insert commands into **one atomic transaction per batch**, with one confirmed-WAL sync before acknowledgements. It does not group already-open independent transactions or separate WAL confirmations. One invalid duplicate rolls back its whole batch. Commit/I/O failure stops the writer; lost IPC replies remain indeterminate, with no automatic retry or durable inbox. Same-collection engine-level group commit requires a separate lock/publication/recovery design. The IPC proof owns exclusive Direct admission for its lifetime and only exposes writes; other processes cannot open ordinary Direct/Shared readers alongside it. A usable service needs a read/snapshot API or integration with the existing coordinator.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	**Safety evidence:** 17 controller scenarios pass, including no early acknowledgement, exact commit-sync counting, batch rollback, queue saturation/drain, partial I/O and failed/post-sync errors, encrypted durable-image recovery, real process kills, truncated IPC frames and a durable write with a lost reply. The current library also passes 102 relevant storage/failure/process regressions. Viable library variants pass their relevant net8.0/net10.0 suites (116–149 tests per partition; child reuse also passes 82 Shared tests); all production library targets build. The naive inline-close failure is why that option is rejected. These are local Linux proofs, not Windows/macOS validation or hosted-CI claims for the alternative branches.
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	
Safety section	Check the description against the implicated contracts	The archive retains all **240 measured processes**: 60 upstream comparisons, 84 ownership comparisons and 96 durable-write runs. These historical results motivated holder/wrapper reuse. The current implementation and fresh measurements are above; the other options remain separate.
